{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AFSiZNsrkaprq8chyeZKRo","type":"tool_result","content":"package controller\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"sync/atomic\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"testing/synctest\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n)\n\nconst iv = 5 * time.Minute\n\nfunc TestFirstAndLaterTicks(t *testing.T) {\n\tsynctest.Test(t, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\tlog, _ := newLog()\n\t\tl := &testLoop{name: \"a\", claims: true}\n\t\tbegin := time.Now()\n\t\tstop := start(t, mustNew(t, Deps{Log: log, Rand: fixedRand(0.5)}, l))\n\t\ttime.Sleep(iv * 3)\n\t\tif err := stop(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif got := l.starts[0].Sub(begin); got != iv/20 { // 0.5 * 10% of the interval\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"first tick after %v, want %v\", got, iv/20)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, g := range l.gaps() {\n\t\t\tif g != iv { // jitter factor 0.9+0.2*0.5 = 1\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"gap %v, want %v\", g, iv)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif l.ticks() < 3 {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"ticks = %d, want >= 3\", l.ticks())\n\t\t}\n\t})\n}\n\nfunc TestNoOverlapWhenTickIsSlow(t *testing.T) {\n\tsynctest.Test(t, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\tlog, _ := newLog()\n\t\tl := &testLoop{name: \"slow\", tick: func(ctx context.Context, _ Env) error {\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(2 * iv)\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}, interval: func(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return iv }}\n\t\t// tick timeout defaults to the interval, so the sleep is cut short\n\t\t// only if the loop honours ctx; here it does not, which is the point.\n\t\tstop := start(t, mustNew(t, Deps{Log: log, Rand: fixedRand(0.5)}, l))\n\t\ttime.Sleep(iv * 20)\n\t\t_ = stop()\n\t\tif l.maxCur != 1 {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"max concurrent ticks = %d, want 1\", l.maxCur)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif l.ticks() < 3 {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"ticks = %d\", l.ticks())\n\t\t}\n\t})\n}\n\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:21:func (l *logBuf) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:27:func (l *logBuf) String() string {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:33:func (l *logBuf) count(sub string) int { return strings.Count(l.String(), sub) }\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:35:func newLog() (*slog.Logger, *logBuf) {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:54:func (l *testLoop) Name() string { return l.name }\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:55:func (l *testLoop) Claims() bool { return l.claims }\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:56:func (l *testLoop) Interval(c *config.Resolved) time.Duration {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:63:func (l *testLoop) Tick(ctx context.Context, env Env) error {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:81:func (l *testLoop) ticks() int {\ninternal/controller/helpers_test.go:88:func (l *testLoop) gaps() []time.Duration {\n     `ard:review:eng-review:done` or `:changes`\n6. **Merge** the PR by hand once you are satisfied: the worker opens it as a\n   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\n   **Squash and merge**. Stop `serve` with Ctrl-C (SIGINT); it stops cleanly\n   between jobs.\n\n**Moving faster than the poll.** Each loop ticks once at startup, then every\ninterval (triage 15 min, workers and reviewers 5 min). Until #161 adds a wake\nsignal, restarting `serve` when no job is running (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM jobs\nWHERE status = 'running'` is 0) makes the next stage start within seconds.\n`ard:approved` counts as soon as triage has finished, so there is no need to\nwait for the \"ready for approval\" comment.\n\n### Manual checks folded into the smoke run\n\n| From | Check | How |\n- #53 Gate 3: half of scanner issues merge untouched\n- #89 Optional gitleaks pass in the log secret scan\n- #138 closeout: don't revert newer plan.md sections committed after a job's base\n- #142 Workers: .gitattributes changes can hide diffs from review\n- #160 eng-review should run the repository's own lint target\n- #161 Wake the loops without restarting ard serve\n- #174 