{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKtxmSohxPnSppLVvQxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`kill -USR1 <pid of ard serve>` now makes every loop run one tick immediately, without a restart. The tick still goes through the config reload, the kill switch and the job pool, and it is logged as `controller.wake`.\n\nI ran `go vet`, `gofmt -l` and `go test` on `internal/controller` and `internal/servecmd`; all pass. I did not run the full `make test` or `make lint`.\n\n- **Wake path:** A new `Deps.Wake` channel in `controller.go` and `scheduler.go` carries the signal. Wakes that arrive while a tick is running or already pending collapse into one extra tick, and a wake during shutdown starts nothing.\n- **Signal handling:** `wake_unix.go` forwards `SIGUSR1` into that channel and is set in `serve.go`. `wake_other.go` returns nil, so the signal does nothing off Unix.\n- **Tests:** I added scheduler tests for tick-now, kill switch, coalescing without overlap and wake after stop. I also added a `SIGUSR1` delivery test for `wakeSignals`.\n- **Docs:** The proposal's kill-switch paragraph and the Gate 2 runbook now describe the signal. The runbook's restart advice is replaced by `kill -USR1`, and #161 is removed from `docs/TODO.md`.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/161/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":31153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":585},"output_tokens":471,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b568cb7-6c40-4f66-b76d-4b3bb13d5c28","uuid":"2709a977-80ac-4338-b2fa-1f1616e91244","timestamp":"2026-11-23T12:56:29.847Z","request_id":"req_011ChKtxmHtBTX1DJmaCSMWU"}
